cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TSVerseHub in research or teaching, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "TSVerseHub: A Verified, Interactive Curriculum for the TypeScript Type System"
abstract: >-
  TSVerseHub is an interactive learning platform for TypeScript whose teaching
  material is machine-checked against the compiler. It contributes (1) a
  dependency-free type-level algebra with documented cost models, including a
  type-level parser and evaluator; (2) an in-memory compiler kernel over the
  TypeScript Compiler API that runs identically in Node and the browser;
  (3) a curriculum model in which every code sample carries a verifiable
  expectation (compiles, fails with specific diagnostics, or infers a stated
  type) and prerequisites form a verified DAG; and (4) a reproducible
  benchmark suite characterising type-checker cost as a function of
  type-level recursion depth.
